{"id": "sc900_p3_q021", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "security_compliance_identity", "objective": "identity_concepts", "subobjective": "authorization", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "After authentication succeeds, a system still needs to decide whether the signed-in identity may perform an action. What is that decision called?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Authorization"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Federation metadata publishing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hashing a password at rest"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Issuing a sensitivity label"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Authorization is the decision about what an already authenticated identity is allowed to do. Federation metadata, hashing, and sensitivity labels are not that access-decision step.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"], "tags": ["authorization", "authorization"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "authorization", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-principles-concepts/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-identity_concepts", "semantic_family_id": "authorization", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q022", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_access_management", "subobjective": "Microsoft Entra Conditional Access", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "What is the role of Microsoft Entra Conditional Access in an access decision?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "It stores customer secrets and TLS certificates for Azure applications"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It evaluates signals such as user, device, location, application, and risk, then applies policy before access is granted"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It classifies Microsoft 365 documents as records"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It provides browser-based RDP connectivity to virtual machines"}], "correct_answer": "b", "explanation": "Conditional Access is the Microsoft Entra policy engine that uses contextual signals to decide whether to allow, block, or require additional controls before access is granted. Key Vault, records management, and Bastion are different services.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"], "tags": ["Microsoft Entra Conditional Access", "conditional_access"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "conditional_access", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_access_management", "semantic_family_id": "conditional_access_policy_engine", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q023", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_authentication", "subobjective": "authentication methods", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Which Microsoft Entra authentication method uses the Microsoft Authenticator app or a similar registered authenticator to approve a sign-in without relying on a password as the primary factor?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "A Microsoft Purview eDiscovery hold"}, {"id": "b", "text": "An Azure Firewall application rule"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Passwordless phone sign-in with Microsoft Authenticator"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A compliance score improvement action"}], "correct_answer": "c", "explanation": "Microsoft Authenticator passwordless phone sign-in is an Entra authentication method. eDiscovery holds, firewall rules, and compliance-score actions are not methods for proving identity at sign-in.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"], "tags": ["authentication methods", "authentication_methods"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "authentication_methods", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_authentication", "semantic_family_id": "authentication_methods_authenticator", "stem_style": "capability_selection", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q024", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_identity_protection_governance", "subobjective": "access reviews", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Why would an organization use Microsoft Entra access reviews as part of identity governance?", "choices": [{"id": "b", "text": "To mitigate volumetric DDoS floods against public IP addresses"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To publish Microsoft's independent audit reports"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To scan email attachments for malware"}, {"id": "a", "text": "To recertify whether existing access should continue and remove access that is no longer needed"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Access reviews help reviewers confirm whether users still need group, application, or privileged access and support removal of stale access. They are not DDoS, Service Trust Portal, or email-threat controls.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"], "tags": ["access reviews", "access_reviews"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "access_reviews", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_identity_protection_governance", "semantic_family_id": "access_reviews", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q025", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "azure_infrastructure_security", "subobjective": "Azure Firewall", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A hub virtual network must apply outbound FQDN-based application rules for traffic leaving multiple spoke networks. Which Azure service is designed for that centralized filtering?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Azure Firewall"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Entra ID Protection"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Purview Activity explorer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Microsoft Defender for Identity"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Azure Firewall can sit in a hub and use application rules, including FQDN-based filtering, to inspect traffic from spoke networks. Identity Protection, Activity explorer, and Defender for Identity do not provide that network filtering.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"], "tags": ["Azure Firewall", "azure_firewall"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "azure_firewall", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-azure_infrastructure_security", "semantic_family_id": "azure_firewall_fqdn_hub", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q026", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "defender_xdr", "subobjective": "Microsoft Defender for Office 365", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Safe Links and Safe Attachments are used to inspect potentially harmful URLs and files in Microsoft 365. Which Defender service provides those protections?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Azure Key Vault"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Defender for Office 365"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Entra Domain Services"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Azure Bastion"}], "correct_answer": "b", "explanation": "Microsoft Defender for Office 365 includes capabilities such as Safe Links and Safe Attachments to help protect email and collaboration content from malicious URLs and files. The other services do not provide those Microsoft 365 collaboration protections.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"], "tags": ["Microsoft Defender for Office 365", "defender_for_office_365"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "defender_for_office_365", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-defender_xdr", "semantic_family_id": "defender_for_office_365_safe_links", "stem_style": "capability_selection", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q027", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "azure_security_management", "subobjective": "Cloud Security Posture Management", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "What is the primary goal of cloud security posture management?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "To collect email authentication methods for guest users"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To replace network security groups with sensitivity labels"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To continuously identify misconfigurations and recommend improvements before they become incidents"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To issue Temporary Access Pass credentials"}], "correct_answer": "c", "explanation": "CSPM is concerned with continuously assessing cloud configuration and recommending posture improvements. It is not an authentication-method, labeling, or TAP capability.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"], "tags": ["Cloud Security Posture Management", "cloud_security_posture_management"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "cloud_security_posture_management", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-azure_security_management", "semantic_family_id": "cloud_security_posture_management", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q028", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_compliance_solutions", "objective": "purview_information_protection_lifecycle", "subobjective": "Content explorer and Activity explorer", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A data-protection analyst needs to see where sensitive or labeled items currently exist across supported locations. Which Microsoft Purview tool is designed for that current-state view?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Azure DDoS Protection"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Defender for Endpoint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Content explorer"}], "correct_answer": "d", "explanation": "Content explorer is the Purview data-classification tool used to browse where sensitive and labeled content currently exists. Activity explorer instead emphasizes historical activity on labeled content, and the other services are unrelated.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/data-classification-activity-explorer"], "tags": ["Content explorer and Activity explorer", "content_and_activity_explorer"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/data-classification-activity-explorer"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "content_and_activity_explorer", "source_authority": "microsoft_documentation", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/data-classification-activity-explorer"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "product-purview-activity-explorer", "semantic_family_id": "content_explorer_current_locations", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q029", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_compliance_solutions", "objective": "purview_compliance_management", "subobjective": "Microsoft Purview portal", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "What is the Microsoft Purview portal designed to provide for compliance and data-governance teams?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "A central workspace for accessing Microsoft Purview risk, compliance, and data-governance capabilities"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A SIEM workspace for ingesting firewall logs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A jump host for RDP into Azure virtual machines"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A public DDoS scrubbing network"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "The Microsoft Purview portal is the central interface for Purview compliance, risk, and data-governance capabilities. Sentinel, Bastion, and DDoS Protection provide different security functions.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "tags": ["Microsoft Purview portal", "purview_portal"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "purview_portal", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-purview_compliance_management", "semantic_family_id": "purview_portal", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q030", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_compliance_solutions", "objective": "purview_insider_risk_ediscovery_audit", "subobjective": "eDiscovery", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A legal hold must keep potentially relevant Microsoft 365 content from being deleted while a case is active. Which Microsoft Purview solution is designed for that case-centered preservation and review work?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Entra password protection"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Purview eDiscovery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Azure Web Application Firewall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Microsoft Defender Vulnerability Management"}], "correct_answer": "b", "explanation": "Microsoft Purview eDiscovery supports placing content on hold in a case and then searching and reviewing that content. Password protection, WAF, and vulnerability management are not eDiscovery case tools.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "tags": ["eDiscovery", "ediscovery"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-03", "blueprint_leaf_id": "ediscovery", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-purview_insider_risk_ediscovery_audit", "semantic_family_id": "ediscovery_legal_hold", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
